output it restates; treat this as a fail.{% endif %}

## Pass

Every factual claim the change adds or alters is supported by the cited output — the SAME
claim, faithfully paraphrased or verbatim, not a nearby or related one the
source happens to also contain.

## Fail

- An added or altered claim states something no cited output says (a plausible-sounding
  fabrication next to a real citation).
- A claim overstates or sharpens what the source says (the source hedges, the
  file asserts), or gets a detail wrong (a version, a default, a name).
- A claim rests on a source the commits do not cite.
- A cited output was not read from a source at all: its <call> only printed the
  words the file now claims (an `echo`, a `printf`, a heredoc), so it proves
  nothing about what any source says.

Name the specific claim and quote the cited output it diverges from, or say
that none supports it.
